WEBVTT

1
00:00:28.458 --> 00:00:31.958
In the opening verses of Chapter 15,

2
00:00:31.958 --> 00:00:34.583
Lord Krishna compared this world

3
00:00:34.583 --> 00:00:37.000
to the inverted Ashwattha tree –

4
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:40.166
with roots above and branches below.

5
00:00:40.166 --> 00:00:41.041
This tree

6
00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:43.000
represents the entanglements

7
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.333
and illusions of the material world.

8
00:00:45.333 --> 00:00:49.666
Now in verse 15.6 He describes
that supreme abode –

9
00:00:49.666 --> 00:00:52.250
upon reaching which the jivatma

10
00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:55.875
is forever freed from this entanglement.

11
00:01:00.541 --> 00:01:03.291
This is one of the most captivating

12
00:01:03.291 --> 00:01:05.583
verses of the Gita.

13
00:01:05.583 --> 00:01:09.416
Lord Krishna says – ‘Na tad bhasayate

14
00:01:09.416 --> 00:01:12.708
suryo na shashankona pavakah.’

15
00:01:12.708 --> 00:01:14.041
His supreme abode

16
00:01:14.041 --> 00:01:15.791
is not illuminated by the sun, moon,

17
00:01:15.791 --> 00:01:18.250
or fire.

18
00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:19.583
That abode needs no

19
00:01:19.583 --> 00:01:22.833
external light,

20
00:01:22.833 --> 00:01:25.791
because it is self-luminous.

21
00:01:25.791 --> 00:01:29.000
There is no darkness there – neither literal,

22
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.166
nor symbolic.

23
00:01:31.166 --> 00:01:33.000
Just as a lamp is not needed

24
00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:35.500
in daylight,

25
00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:36.416
in the same way

26
00:01:36.416 --> 00:01:38.333
the light sources

27
00:01:38.333 --> 00:01:40.041
we depend on here

28
00:01:40.041 --> 00:01:44.041
are not needed in that spiritual realm.

29
00:01:44.041 --> 00:01:46.291
Tad dhama paramam mama –

30
00:01:46.291 --> 00:01:48.791
this is My supreme abode.

31
00:01:48.791 --> 00:01:52.416
Lord Krishna is speaking not only of a place,

32
00:01:52.416 --> 00:01:55.625
but of His divine world –

33
00:01:55.625 --> 00:01:57.541
filled with His eternal companions

34
00:01:57.541 --> 00:02:01.000
and divine pastimes.

35
00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:03.625
Yad gatva na nivartante –

36
00:02:03.625 --> 00:02:06.333
one who attains this abode

37
00:02:06.333 --> 00:02:10.916
never returns to this material world.

38
00:02:10.916 --> 00:02:14.208
There is no cycle of rebirth here.

39
00:02:14.208 --> 00:02:17.250
No need to change bodies,

40
00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:19.125
no temporary pleasures,

41
00:02:19.125 --> 00:02:22.625
no repeated suffering.

42
00:02:22.625 --> 00:02:27.000
The soul finally arrives home.

43
00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:27.958
This verse

44
00:02:27.958 --> 00:02:31.208
can be understood literally, but

45
00:02:31.208 --> 00:02:34.583
it also carries deep symbolism.

46
00:02:34.583 --> 00:02:37.833
The sun shows us forms –

47
00:02:37.833 --> 00:02:39.750
so this abode cannot be seen

48
00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:42.458
with material eyes.

49
00:02:42.458 --> 00:02:45.458
The moon governs the mind –

50
00:02:45.458 --> 00:02:47.291
so it cannot be felt

51
00:02:47.291 --> 00:02:49.708
through imagination.

52
00:02:49.708 --> 00:02:52.625
Fire is the symbol of speech –

53
00:02:52.625 --> 00:02:54.333
so this abode cannot be

54
00:02:54.333 --> 00:02:57.375
fully expressed in words.

55
00:02:57.375 --> 00:03:01.041
It is beyond the senses, mind, and intellect.

56
00:03:01.041 --> 00:03:02.916
It can only be experienced

57
00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:07.166
through pure devotion.

58
00:03:07.166 --> 00:03:10.500
We keep wandering on the branches of

59
00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:12.208
.

60
00:03:12.208 --> 00:03:15.166
from one attachment to another,

61
00:03:15.166 --> 00:03:18.166
one desire to another,

62
00:03:18.166 --> 00:03:20.458
one work to another,

63
00:03:20.458 --> 00:03:22.833
one place to another,

64
00:03:22.833 --> 00:03:25.541
one joy to another,

65
00:03:25.541 --> 00:03:26.916
thinking -

66
00:03:26.916 --> 00:03:30.250
something better lies ahead.

67
00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:33.041
But Lord Krishna tells us –

68
00:03:33.041 --> 00:03:36.583
beyond this tree lies another abode –

69
00:03:36.583 --> 00:03:41.708
a place of peace and steadiness.

70
00:03:41.708 --> 00:03:44.083
This verse encourages us –

71
00:03:44.083 --> 00:03:45.083
even if detachment

72
00:03:45.083 --> 00:03:48.166
feels difficult, even if surrender feels far away,

73
00:03:48.166 --> 00:03:49.041
simply

74
00:03:49.041 --> 00:03:51.708
knowing that such a beautiful,

75
00:03:51.708 --> 00:03:54.375
eternal, welcoming place exists –

76
00:03:54.375 --> 00:03:55.958
one that belongs to Lord Krishna –

77
00:03:55.958 --> 00:03:59.000
can awaken hope in our hearts.

78
00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:03.375
And the moment we desire it with all our heart,

79
00:04:03.375 --> 00:04:06.916
this journey toward liberation begins.

80
00:04:11.708 --> 00:04:12.916
Sometimes

81
00:04:12.916 --> 00:04:17.000
you hear something – that feels very far,

82
00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:22.500
very vast, and almost unbelievable.

83
00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:25.291
Is there truly a place

84
00:04:25.291 --> 00:04:26.583
where neither sun

85
00:04:26.583 --> 00:04:30.000
nor fire is needed?

86
00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.458
Is there really an abode

87
00:04:32.458 --> 00:04:33.625
where the cycle of birth

88
00:04:33.625 --> 00:04:36.833
and death ends?

89
00:04:36.833 --> 00:04:40.791
Your first thought may be –

90
00:04:40.791 --> 00:04:44.375
‘Can this really be true?’

91
00:04:44.375 --> 00:04:46.541
For example –

92
00:04:46.541 --> 00:04:49.291
when a serious illness cannot be treated

93
00:04:49.291 --> 00:04:53.041
in a small town, it feels

94
00:04:53.041 --> 00:04:56.500
as though it will never be cured.

95
00:04:56.500 --> 00:04:59.583
But when news comes

96
00:04:59.583 --> 00:05:03.208
of a specialist hospital in a larger city,

97
00:05:03.208 --> 00:05:08.416
what seemed impossible suddenly
becomes a possibility.

98
00:05:08.416 --> 00:05:13.625
In the same way, do not confine
yourself to limitations.

99
00:05:13.625 --> 00:05:18.125
Inspiration often comes from an
unimaginable source –

100
00:05:18.125 --> 00:05:23.333
just keep your heart open to it.

101
00:05:23.333 --> 00:05:26.833
Not being able to understand
something right now

102
00:05:26.833 --> 00:05:31.000
does not mean it is untrue.

103
00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:34.291
It only shows

104
00:05:34.291 --> 00:05:36.500
the limits of understanding

105
00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:39.125
from where you currently stand.

106
00:05:39.125 --> 00:05:44.375
When I speak of My eternal abode,

107
00:05:44.375 --> 00:05:45.458
I do not ask you

108
00:05:45.458 --> 00:05:49.541
to imagine it.

109
00:05:49.541 --> 00:05:51.791
I ask you –

110
00:05:51.791 --> 00:05:56.791
accept it with your true heart.

111
00:05:56.791 --> 00:05:58.791
Such knowledge

112
00:05:58.791 --> 00:06:01.791
expands your vision.

113
00:06:01.791 --> 00:06:04.291
It reminds you

114
00:06:04.291 --> 00:06:07.625
that life is far more than daily routine,

115
00:06:07.625 --> 00:06:10.791
success, and failure.

116
00:06:10.791 --> 00:06:13.416
It shows you what

117
00:06:13.416 --> 00:06:17.166
your soul already longs for –

118
00:06:17.166 --> 00:06:22.875
even if your mind has not understood it yet.

119
00:06:22.875 --> 00:06:25.125
Your first response?

120
00:06:25.125 --> 00:06:28.833
Not doubt – it should be curiosity.

121
00:06:28.833 --> 00:06:32.333
What feels far today

122
00:06:32.333 --> 00:06:36.000
can become your home tomorrow –

123
00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:39.750
if you allow yourself

124
00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:42.541
to move toward it.

125
00:06:47.166 --> 00:06:49.583
In families, everyone wants –

126
00:06:49.583 --> 00:06:51.166
to be heard,

127
00:06:51.166 --> 00:06:53.833
understood, and respected.

128
00:06:53.833 --> 00:06:57.791
But sometimes, in the rush to solve problems

129
00:06:57.791 --> 00:07:00.541
or prove a point,

130
00:07:00.541 --> 00:07:03.583
we forget – that peace

131
00:07:03.583 --> 00:07:07.250
does not come from winning arguments,

132
00:07:07.250 --> 00:07:12.375
but from having the courage to look beyond

133
00:07:12.375 --> 00:07:14.000
the familiar.

134
00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:18.666
I said – My eternal abode is not

135
00:07:18.666 --> 00:07:20.625
illuminated by the sun,

136
00:07:20.625 --> 00:07:24.125
moon, or fire.

137
00:07:24.125 --> 00:07:28.583
This means – what truly matters

138
00:07:28.583 --> 00:07:30.375
may be beyond the reach

139
00:07:30.375 --> 00:07:34.000
of your senses and experience.

140
00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:38.458
In the family, a real solution begins

141
00:07:38.458 --> 00:07:42.166
when someone pauses and says –

142
00:07:42.166 --> 00:07:45.166
‘Perhaps there is another way.

143
00:07:45.166 --> 00:07:48.333
Perhaps we have not thought of everything.’

144
00:07:48.333 --> 00:07:50.291
This is where humility comes –

145
00:07:50.291 --> 00:07:52.625
and with it, light.

146
00:07:52.625 --> 00:07:57.500
Do not treat your own perspective
as the complete picture.

147
00:07:57.500 --> 00:08:03.333
Do not dismiss what you cannot
understand right now.

148
00:08:03.333 --> 00:08:06.333
Because what is unknown today

149
00:08:06.333 --> 00:08:10.083
may be the very thing that fulfils

150
00:08:10.083 --> 00:08:13.125
your family’s long-unmet need.

151
00:08:17.791 --> 00:08:20.666
At the workplace you are taught –

152
00:08:20.666 --> 00:08:22.750
to plan, analyse,

153
00:08:22.750 --> 00:08:25.625
and predict the future.

154
00:08:25.625 --> 00:08:28.625
But the deepest solutions

155
00:08:28.625 --> 00:08:32.625
do not always come from what
you already know –

156
00:08:32.625 --> 00:08:37.916
they come from what you have
never even considered.

157
00:08:37.916 --> 00:08:42.000
I said – My eternal abode is not illuminated

158
00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:45.166
by the sun, moon,

159
00:08:45.166 --> 00:08:47.666
and fire.

160
00:08:47.666 --> 00:08:50.166
In simple terms –

161
00:08:50.166 --> 00:08:52.833
what truly matters

162
00:08:52.833 --> 00:08:54.250
is not always visible

163
00:08:54.250 --> 00:08:58.125
through your familiar methods.

164
00:08:58.125 --> 00:09:02.000
The best strategies are born

165
00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:05.625
when leadership creates space fo
reflection, humility,

166
00:09:05.625 --> 00:09:09.125
and deep listening.

167
00:09:09.125 --> 00:09:10.125
When you

168
00:09:10.125 --> 00:09:14.375
let go of the insistence to control every outcome,

169
00:09:14.375 --> 00:09:18.416
and accept what lies

170
00:09:18.416 --> 00:09:20.875
beyond logic –

171
00:09:20.875 --> 00:09:24.291
new paths reveal themselves.

172
00:09:24.291 --> 00:09:26.333
Sometimes this means

173
00:09:26.333 --> 00:09:30.125
trusting your inner voice.

174
00:09:30.125 --> 00:09:31.666
Sometimes it means

175
00:09:31.666 --> 00:09:35.083
listening to the quietest voice in the room –

176
00:09:35.083 --> 00:09:38.666
the one everyone else has ignored.

177
00:09:38.666 --> 00:09:41.875
Do not let your experience

178
00:09:41.875 --> 00:09:44.958
become a blindfold.

179
00:09:44.958 --> 00:09:50.500
Let it become the foundation for a
new way of seeing.

180
00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:54.291
The unknown is not your enemy –

181
00:09:54.291 --> 00:09:58.875
it may be exactly the missing piece

182
00:09:58.875 --> 00:10:02.208
you need.

183
00:10:02.208 --> 00:10:05.125
Work done with this openness

184
00:10:05.125 --> 00:10:09.583
does not remain limited to solving problems.

185
00:10:09.583 --> 00:10:13.708
It becomes a larger discovery –

186
00:10:13.708 --> 00:10:17.833
one that carries you toward real growth.
